Cell["\<\
This form is flexible, convenient for input and is very intuitive. \
Unfortunately, it becomes not so attractive when we need to expand MV \
products, since we have to define many slow rules how to manipulate \
coefficients of expressions. A much faster way to expand products (especially \
with symbolic coefficients) is to convert expressions into Associations, \
where indices play the role of keys and the coefficients become values. This \
considerably reduces complexity and makes product expansion many times \
faster. For example, define few symbolic MVs and expand their product\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->True,
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.954599763647778*^9, 3.9545997702428703`*^9}, {
  3.9580249314074163`*^9, 3.95802496582027*^9}, {3.9580401154561653`*^9, 
  3.958040183713418*^9}, {3.960119531788331*^9, 3.960119695387149*^9}, {
  3.9601197325737553`*^9, 3.9601204521588583`*^9}},
 CellID->569233702,ExpressionUUID->"2b2b0ac9-c484-4d07-9c32-72a33cc74298"],

